# Entity Grid Pattern

Grids compose `@entity-framework` primitives. Feature code wires providers and renders `<EntityGrid>` — it does not reimplement tables.

A routed list page renders its grid **inline on the page**, not inside a modal (see `nextjs-list-pages.mdc`).

## Folder structure

```
{feature}-grid/   (or manage-{entity}/)
  {Feature}Grid.tsx                 # thin wrapper
  use-{feature}-grid.ts(x)          # optional hook owning config + actions
  {feature}-grid.config.ts          # static EntityGridConfig fields (optional)
  columns/
    {feature}-grid-columns.ts(x)
  state/
    models/
    {feature}-search.data-provider.ts
```

Shared across the feature area:

```
shared/state/{feature}-update.service.ts
shared/utils/{feature}-routes.ts
```

## Wiring

```tsx
const { searchState, authInFlight, isAuthenticated } = useAuthenticatedEntitySearch(
  searchProvider,
  defaultSearch
);
const gridState = useEntityGridState(gridConfig, columns, searchState, updateService);

return (
  <EntityGridAuthGate authInFlight={authInFlight} isAuthenticated={isAuthenticated}>
    <EntityGrid gridState={gridState} headerActions={...} />
  </EntityGridAuthGate>
);
```

Local (non-URL) search: `useAuthenticatedEntitySearchLocal`.

## Grid config

`EntityGridConfig` should set:

- `tid`, `defaultSortColumn`, `pageSize`, `hasPaging`
- `rowActions` / `rowActionsDisplay: 'menu'` when using overflow menus (rendered by `DropdownMenu`, portalled so it is never clipped by the table)
- `prefetchHref` on row actions that open a route (Edit) — `EntityGrid` prefetches it on hover / focus
- `headerToolbarActions` for Add / primary toolbar actions
- Add / Edit open the form modal via `useModalNavigate().open(href)` (the grid itself stays on the page)

## Columns

Define in `columns/{feature}-grid-columns.ts(x)`. Keep `headerLabel` / `propertyName` meaningful. Use framework cell helpers from `@entity-framework` where available; action menus via config `rowActions`, not ad-hoc button columns.

## Refresh after mutations

```ts
updateService.trigger(); // after create/update/delete
```

Grid state subscribes through `useEntityGridState(..., updateService)`.

